#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In the general formulation of quantum information, operations on quantum states are represented by a special class of mappings called *channels*.\n"
"This includes useful operations, such as ones corresponding to unitary gates and circuits, as well as operations we deem as noise and would prefer to avoid.\n"
"We can also describe measurements as channels, which we'll do in the next lesson.\n"
"In short, any <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"A discrete-time change refers to one occurring between two distinct moments in time, as opposed to a continuous process that can be described over infinitesimally small time periods.\">discrete-time</DefinitionTooltip> change in states that is physically realizable (in an idealized sense) can be described by a channel.\n"
msgstr ""
"Dalam formulasi umum informasi kuantum, operasi pada status kuantum direpresentasikan oleh kelas pemetaan khusus yang disebut *channel*.\n"
"Ini mencakup operasi yang berguna, seperti yang bersesuaian dengan gate dan sirkuit uniter, serta operasi yang kita anggap sebagai noise dan ingin kita hindari.\n"
"Kita juga bisa mendeskripsikan pengukuran sebagai channel, yang akan kita lakukan di pelajaran berikutnya.\n"
"Singkatnya, perubahan status apa pun yang <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Perubahan diskrit-waktu mengacu pada perubahan yang terjadi antara dua momen waktu yang berbeda, berbeda dengan proses kontinu yang bisa dideskripsikan selama periode waktu yang sangat kecil.\">diskrit-waktu</DefinitionTooltip> dan bisa direalisasikan secara fisik (dalam arti ideal) bisa dideskripsikan oleh channel.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The term *channel* comes to us from information theory, which (among other things) studies the information-carrying capacities of noisy *communication channels*.\n"
"In this context, a quantum channel could specify the quantum state that's received when a given quantum state is sent, perhaps through a quantum network of some sort.\n"
"It should be understood, however, that the terminology merely reflects this historical motivation and is used in a more general way.\n"
"Indeed, we can describe a wide variety of things (such as complicated quantum computations) as channels, even though they have nothing to do with communication and would be unlikely to arise naturally in such a setting.\n"
msgstr ""
"Istilah *channel* berasal dari teori informasi, yang (di antara hal-hal lain) mempelajari kapasitas pembawa informasi dari *saluran komunikasi* yang berisik.\n"
"Dalam konteks ini, channel kuantum bisa menentukan status kuantum yang diterima ketika status kuantum tertentu dikirim, mungkin melalui jaringan kuantum semacam itu.\n"
"Namun harus dipahami bahwa terminologi ini hanya mencerminkan motivasi historis ini dan digunakan secara lebih umum.\n"
"Memang, kita bisa mendeskripsikan berbagai hal (seperti komputasi kuantum yang rumit) sebagai channel, meskipun mereka tidak ada hubungannya dengan komunikasi dan kemungkinan tidak akan muncul secara alami dalam pengaturan seperti itu.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We'll begin the lesson with a discussion of some basic aspects of channels, along with a small selection of examples.\n"
"Then we'll move on to three different ways to represent channels in mathematical terms later in the lesson.\n"
"We'll see that, although these representations are different, they all offer equivalent mathematical characterizations of channels.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kita akan memulai pelajaran dengan diskusi tentang beberapa aspek dasar channel, bersama dengan pilihan kecil contoh.\n"
"Kemudian kita akan beralih ke tiga cara berbeda untuk merepresentasikan channel dalam istilah matematis di bagian pelajaran selanjutnya.\n"
"Kita akan melihat bahwa, meskipun representasi ini berbeda, mereka semua menawarkan karakterisasi matematis channel yang setara.\n"

